# pkglist.apt --- the stuff Nix wouldn't take -*- mode: conf -*-
#
# Apply on a fresh machine with:
#   grep -vE '^\s*(#|$)' packages/maushold/pkglist.apt | xargs sudo apt-get install -y
#
# This file is hand-curated -- edit it by hand. DO NOT `apt-mark showmanual >` over it;
# that re-sorts, drops the comments, and murders every joke below. To spot drift
# between this file and what's actually installed (comments/order ignored), run:
#   apt-drift               # '-' = in here only, '+' = installed only
# (a script in shell/.local/bin/)
#
# Rule 1: Nix first, apt only when Nix can't or won't. Everything below is here
# because it lost that argument. Grouped by what it's for.
#
# Rule 2: see Rule 1.

# bootstrap, chickens brawling with eggs
git                                            # how this repo got here in the first place
stow                                           # how this repo got everywhere else

# (populate the rest from `apt-mark showmanual` on the machine, pruning anything Nix manages)
